<title>AUSTRALIA: SFE wheat futures in tradeless day.</title>
<headline>SFE wheat futures in tradeless day.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wwheat futures were untraded at the Sydney Futures Exchange on Thursday, with local investors ignoring a slightly firmer U.S. market overnight.</p>
<p>The lethargy at the SFE was in contrast to Wednesday, when local trading picked up on the back of declining U.S. futures prices and a tight cash market, leaving most nearby months lower. Despite some rain, Australian weather continued to hold little sway over trade sentiment, a grains trader said.</p>
